(6, '9', 9, 'class="av-devanagari">सुहृन्मित्रार्युदासीनमध्यस्थद्वेष्यबन्धुषु ।
साधुष्वपि च पापेषु समबुद्धिर्विशिष्यते ॥ ९ ॥

<div', 'class="av-verse_text">suhṛn-mitrāry-udāsīna-
madhyastha-dveṣya-bandhuṣu
sādhuṣv api ca pāpeṣu
sama-buddhir viśiṣyate

<div', 'class="av-synonyms">su-hṛt — to well-wishers by nature; mitra — benefactors with affection; ari — enemies; udāsīna — neutrals between belligerents; madhya-stha — mediators between belligerents; dveṣya — the envious; bandhuṣu — and the relatives or well-wishers; sādhuṣu — unto the pious; api — as well as; ca — and; pāpeṣu — unto the sinners; sama-buddhiḥ — having equal intelligence; viśiṣyate — is far advanced.

<div', 'class="av-translation">A person is considered still further advanced when he regards honest well-wishers, affectionate benefactors, the neutral, mediators, the envious, friends and enemies, the pious and the sinners all with an equal mind.

TEXT 8TEXT 10

DonateThanks to Shweta Saxena; Gopalakrishnan Soundarajan;    Kuldip Persaud;  Raghava Chandra Dasa; Shubhangi Rajiv Panjiyar; Suparna Kotaru;  Rajendra and Geeta Ramchandani;  Jaykumar Prabhakar; Bharat Vyas; Shri Chander Mohan Gilhotra, HG Prashant Mukund Das, Shri Trilok Singh Grover, HG Bhakta Mitra Das, Laxmi Narayan Agarwal; Ronak Talati; Bhargav Ashok; Akiralali; Rajasa das; Riya and Tejal Chopade; Indradyumna Swami; Jai Devaki Parks;  Ashmi Chakraborty; Hari-kirtana das; Ramesta das; Prasad Buddhavarapu; Kresna Sucandra; Esekiel Jaggernauth and all others for supporting this site.

His Divine Grace A.C. Bhaktivedanta Swami Prabhupāda, Founder-Ācārya of the International Society for Krishna Consciousness.
