th\":\"/en/library/bg/6/13-14/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"समं कायशिरोग्रीवं धारयन्नचलं स्थिर: ।
सम्प्रेक्ष्य नासिकाग्रं स्वं दिशश्चानवलोकयन् ॥ १३ ॥
प्रशान्तात्मा विगतभीर्ब्रह्मचारिव्रते स्थित: ।
मन: संयम्य मच्च‍ित्तो युक्त आसीत मत्पर: ॥ १४ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1839,\"bb\":1626,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/13-14/b1626/\",\"body_value\":\"samaṁ kāya-śiro-grīvaṁ
dhārayann acalaṁ sthiraḥ
samprekṣya nāsikāgraṁ svaṁ
diśaś cānavalokayan\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1840,\"bb\":1627,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/13-14/b1627/\",\"body_value\":\"praśāntātmā vigata-bhīr
brahmacāri-vrate sthitaḥ
manaḥ saṁyamya mac-citto
yukta āsīta mat-paraḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":1841,\"bb\":1628,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/13-14/b1628/\",\"shadow_value\":\"samam – straight; kāya – body; śiraḥ – head; grīvam – and neck; dhārayan – holding; acalam – unmoving; sthiraḥ – still; samprekṣya – looking; nāsikā – of the nose; agram – at the tip; svam – own; diśaḥ – on all sides; ca – also; anavalokayan – not looking; praśānta – unagitated; ātmā – mind; vigata-bhīḥ – devoid of fear; brahmacāri-vrate – in the vow of celibacy; sthitaḥ – situated; manaḥ – mind; saṁyamya – completely subduing; mat – upon Me (Kṛṣṇa); cittaḥ – concentrating the mind; yuktaḥ – the actual yogī; āsīta – should sit; mat – Me; paraḥ – the ultimate goal.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"samam\",\"translation\":\"straight\"},{\"word\":\"kāya\",\"translation\":\"body\"},{\"word\":\"śiraḥ\",\"translation\":\"head\"},{\"word\":\"grīvam\",\"translation\":\"and neck\"},{\"word\":\"dhārayan\",\"translation\":\"holding\"},{\"word\":\"acalam\",\"translation\":\"unmoving\"},{\"word\":\"sthiraḥ\",\"translation\":\"still\"},{\"word\":\"samprekṣya\",\"translation\":\"looking\"},{\"word\":\"nāsikā\",\"translation\":\"of the nose\"},{\"word\":\"agram\",\"translation\":\"at the tip\"},{\"word\":\"svam\",\"translation\":\"own\"},{\"word\":\"diśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"on all sides\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"anavalokayan\",\"translation\":\"not looking\"},{\"word\":\"praśānta\",\"translation\":\"unagitated\"},{\"word\":\"ātmā\",\"translation\":\"mind\"},{\"word\":\"vigata-bhīḥ\",\"translation\":\"devoid of fear\"},{\"word\":\"brahmacāri-vrate\",\"translation\":\"in the vow of celibacy\"},{\"word\":\"sthitaḥ\",\"translation\":\"situated\"},{\"word\":\"manaḥ\",\"translation\":\"mind\"},{\"word\":\"saṁyamya\",\"translation\":\"completely subduing\"},{\"word\":\"mat\",\"translation\":\"upon Me (Kṛṣṇa)\"},{\"word\":\"cittaḥ\",\"translation\":\"concentrating the mind\"},{\"word\":\"yuktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the actual yogī\"},{\"word\":\"āsīta\",\"translation\":\"should sit\"},{\"word\":\"mat\",\"translation\":\"Me\"},{\"word\":\"paraḥ\",\"translation\":\"the ultimate goal\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1842,\"bb\":1629,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/13-14/b1629/\",\"body_value\":\"One should hold one’s body, neck and head erect in a straight line and stare steadily at the tip of the nose. Thus, with an unagitated, subdued mind, devoid of fear, completely free from sex life, one should meditate upon Me within the heart and make Me the ultimate goal of life.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1843,\"bb\":1630,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/13-14/b1630/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1844,\"bb\":1631,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/13-14/b1631/\",\"body_value\":\"karmaṇā manasā vācā
sarvāvasthāsu sarvadā
sarvatra maithuna-tyāgo
