nirāhārasya dehinaḥ
rasa-varjaṁ raso ’py asya
paraṁ dṛṣṭvā nivartate\"}}]}]\n44:[\"$\",\"$L2b\",\"child-1847\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:4\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Whereas others are forced to restrain themselves from sense gratification, a devotee of the Lord automatically refrains because of superior taste. Other than the devotee, no one has any information of that superior taste.\"}}]}]\n45:[\"$\",\"$L2b\",\"child-1848\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:5\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Vigata-bhīḥ.\"}],\" One cannot be fearless unless one is fully in Kṛṣṇa consciousness. A conditioned soul is fearful due to his perverted memory, his forgetfulness of his eternal relationship with Kṛṣṇa. The \",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"2\",{\"href\":\"/en/library/sb/11/2/37/\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Bhāgavatam\"}],\" (11.2.37)\"]}],\" says, \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"4\",{\"children\":\"bhayaṁ dvitīyābhiniveśataḥ syād īśād apetasya viparyayo ’smṛtiḥ.\"}],\" Kṛṣṇa consciousness is the only basis for fearlessness. Therefore, perfect practice is possible for a person who is Kṛṣṇa conscious. And since the ultimate goal of \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"6\",{\"children\":\"yoga\"}],\" practice is to see the Lord within, a Kṛṣṇa conscious person is already the best of all \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"8\",{\"children\":\"yogīs.\"}],\" The principles of the \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"10\",{\"children\":\"yoga\"}],\" system mentioned herein are different from those of the popular so-called \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"12\",{\"children\":\"yoga\"}],\" societies.\"]}]}]\n"])(function(){function c(){var b=a.contentDocument||(a.contentWindow&&a.contentWindow.document);if(b){var d=b.createElement(''script'